|~ `::snippet`, the kind of a snippet, and the laws declared under it.

   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSSLF#doc]. ~|

:snippet
  |~~ A snippet is a query a page shows its reader to run and see,
      written in the prose of a doc as a quote under this tag:
      ::snippet~(::vec | manifest) lists the verbs of vectors, and
      ::snippet~({:a [5 6]} | get /a/-1) shows a path read. `open`
      runs it, and `snippets` reads the snippets of a doc.

      A snippet answers whatever it shows, a failure among them, since
      it reproduces a situation for its reader; a link opens a page, and
      a law answers true.
      ::link~(::link | doc) ::link~(::qlang/hypertext | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps
        |~~ The query a snippet shows, a quote beneath the tags it is given
            under.
        ~~|
        ::quote
    | proves :opensToWhatItShows
        |~~ A snippet opens to what it shows. ~~|
        ~(|~~ ::snippet~(::vec | manifest) ~~| | snippets | first | open | has ::vec/count)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAString
        |~~ A snippet is a quote. ~~|
        ~(::snippet"x" !| type | eq ::snippet/PayloadKindNotTakenError)

